# ROADMAP_NS_PV2 — Second red-team: sold as product

File: openOODA/audit/roadmap_ns_pv2.oot
Logline: This board names residual and moonshot items that the public site or a board presents as product.
Setup: Survey only. Independent of PV1. No product edit. No ROADMAP edit. Pin v0.200.0-beta. C emit + gcc remains the product path.
Beats:
  1. Compare the door and the guide to SHIPPED.oot.
  2. Compare NORTHSTAR production clauses to ROADMAP leftover rows.
  3. Flag install, SMT, device GPU, HITL, and certified std if sold without proof.
  4. Recommend a 5.2 honesty row only when a stranger meets a lie.

## 1. Method

  Production here means a stranger on the pin can do the job today.
  A 5.1 stay-residual fact is not this-cycle work unless the public site sells it as product.
  Do not open a 5.3 oodac row. Do not open a 5.4 library row.
  Do not copy a MOONSHOTS.oot row into leftover work.
  Proof roots: SHIPPED.oot, ROADMAP.oot, `../ooda/`, `../qa/qa_master.oo`, `../openOODA.github.io/`.

## 2. What is honest

  SHIPPED.oot and ROADMAP.oot name C emit + gcc as the product path.
  Pin is v0.200.0-beta. RAM-cold about 164s. Disk-warm about 0.02s. 179 modules.
  Guide `Use.oot` and `Home.oot` say public install waits.
  Guide `Limits.oot` says const header `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` fold. That is not full SMT.
  Guide `Limits.oot` says two `emit-c` of hello are byte-identical. It does not claim gcc binaries.
  Product std is `ooda/std`. Org `std/` is not certified. The guide does not claim a 4061-file cert.
  `qa/qa_master.oo` header names broken fixtures and `e2e/*.sh` as residual. That matches ROADMAP 5.1.
  `qa/README.oot` says this tree does not certify org `std/`.

## 3. Public site sells residual as product

### 3.1 Install (5.1 stay-residual)

  Door `index.html` first command is `curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install | oo`.
  The next block lists `~/.local/bin/ooda`, `oodac`, `std`, `runtime`, and `env`.
  One line says install waits. The first action and the file list sell a first-machine install.
  WORKFLOW.oot: that line is paused. Do not sell it as a first-machine bootstrap.
  Live `install` is a `.oo` file that prints wait text. It does not place binaries.
  Site `README.oot` still documents `curl … | sh` and pin `v0.183.0-alpha`.
  `../ooda/README.oot` Quickstart is `curl … | sh` and pin `v0.199.0-alpha`. It says beta is not claimed.
  `../ooda/install/BOOTSTRAP_PIN` is `v0.199.0-alpha`. Boards pin `v0.200.0-beta`.

### 3.2 HITL (5.1 stay-residual)

  SHIPPED: HITL is not product. The human loop is `ooda fix`.
  Guide `Use.oot` says: This is the human HITL / fix loop.
  That name sells RP-5.6 (theoretical pause, signed human oracle). The tree has `ooda fix`.

### 3.3 Device GPU (5.1 stay-residual)

  SHIPPED: `GpuCap` CPU / noop launch is product. Device dispatch is residual. Not CUDA.
  Guide `Options.oot` token table: `&GpuCap` lets the function `gpu_launch_shader`.
  `ooda/std/os/gpu.oo` logline: `gpu_launch_shader` never talks to a device.
  The table does not say residual. A stranger reads a device shader launch.

### 3.4 Full SMT and certified std

  Guide Language and Limits do not sell a general symbolic solver. No SMT honesty row.
  Guide does not sell org `std/` as certified. No cert honesty row.

## 4. Public site sells moonshots as product

  Door Defense (present tense):
    Memory layout can change at load. That is a metamorphic binary.
    Call-graph integrity seals approved paths.
    Zero-day stack raises cost with layout change.
  Guide `Safety.oot` §10 repeats the load-time layout change.
  Those claims live in MOONSHOTS.oot §2 and in research papers marked theoretical.
  SHIPPED measured isolate is a hash. It is not SGX / TDX / SEV. It is not layout morph.
  Guide `Research.oot`: Production LLVM — Peak native when you want the long compile.
  RP-4.1.2 says LLVM is the primary production CPU target. The product path is C + gcc.
  Full gcc-parity LLVM is already ROADMAP 5.3. Do not add a 5.3 row. The site lie is 5.2.

## 5. Registry sold as a finished store

  Door Catalog and guide `Packages.oot` teach `ooda add --registry` as a live store.
  ROADMAP §6 OPEN-42 remainder: do not sell the on-disk registry as a finished first-machine store.
  That remainder is not a 5.1 `[ ]` row. The site sells it. Open an honesty row.

## 6. NORTHSTAR production gaps with no leftover

  Merkle AST cache and incremental skip (NORTHSTAR 3.3): not on disk as a compiler cache. Not this-cycle production. No row.
  Isolated actor heaps (NORTHSTAR 1.2): `chs_rt_actor.c` is a pthread plus a mailbox. Not a production hole this cycle. No row.
  Pause-free GC, ghost-state undo, typestate machines, AST macros in expand: later or moonshot. No row.
  WASM browser host: emit-wasm writes a `\0asm` module. Browser runtime is not the product path. No row.
  vscode `ooda-lsp.js` and `qa/e2e/*.sh`: already 5.1. The guide points at `ooda lsp`, which is product.

## 7. Verdict

  Boards SHIPPED and ROADMAP stay honest on SMT, std cert, AArch64, and C + gcc.
  The stranger lie is the door and a few guide lines, plus stale `ooda/README.oot`.
  C emit + gcc remains the product path. Pin v0.200.0-beta.

